<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sima Yi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">179–251</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sima Yi was a general and statesman of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-wei">Cao Wei</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-kingdoms-period">Three Kingdoms period</a>. He defended Wei against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhuge-liang">Zhuge Liang</a>'s northern campaigns, destroyed the Gongsun regime in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a> in 238, and in 249 seized control of the court in a coup against Cao Shuang, laying the foundations for his grandson's Jin dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sima-yi.jpg" alt="Sima Yi" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ming Zhu Tianran · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E9%AD%8F%C2%B7%E5%A4%AA%E5%82%85_%E5%8F%B8%E9%A6%AC%E6%87%BF.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
